<title>USA: Fed stays out of system at usual intervention time.</title>
<headline>Fed stays out of system at usual intervention time.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve stayed out of the banking system during its usual intervention time Tuesday morning.</p>
<p>The lack of action was not unexpected.</p>
<p>The federal funds rate was trading at 5-13/16 percent, versus the current target level of 5.25 percent.</p>
<p>-- John P. Hughes, N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1663</p>
</text>
